  <model metaid="meta_rivaroxaban_liver" id="rivaroxaban_liver" name="Model for hepatic rivaroxaban metabolism." substanceUnits="mmole" timeUnits="min" volumeUnits="litre" areaUnits="m2" lengthUnits="metre" extentUnits="mmole">
    <notes>
      <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <p>Model for hepatic rivaroxaban metabolism.</p>
        <p>Rivaroxaban is metabolized in the liver into a variety of metabolites,
which are lumped (<code>rx</code>): oxidation by CYP3A4 (<code>f_cyp3a4</code>) and CYP2J2 and
CYP independent hydrolysis (Weinz2009, Mueck2014). The metabolites leave
the liver into the plasma, from which they are excreted in the urine, and
with the bile into the feces.</p>
        <p>The content of this model has been carefully created in a manual research effort.</p>
